    "## CONCEPT: Look at your data first\n",
    "\n",
    "- `df.head(n)` shows the first `n` rows (default 5). `df.tail(n)` shows the last rows.\n",
    "- `df.shape` = (rows, columns).\n",
    "- `df.info()` = column names, types, and how many values are **not** missing.\n",
    "- `df.describe()` = count, average, min, max and more for the number columns.\n",
    "- Always do this first. Then you know what is in your data."
   ]
  },
